Third-party components
----------------------

1. Grimace

   Directories: grimace-main/ and share/grimace_from_va/grimace_from_va/vendor/

   Grimace is a comic-style facial expression library. The copy in this
   package keeps its upstream MIT license and attribution:

   - grimace-main/LICENSE
   - grimace-main/README.md
   - share/grimace_from_va/grimace_from_va/vendor/LICENSE.grimace

   Upstream: https://github.com/grimace-project/web
   Copyright (c) 2018, as stated in that LICENSE.
   The vendored LICENSE files are unchanged.

2. NRC Valence, Arousal, and Dominance (VAD) Lexicon

   Creator: Dr. Saif M. Mohammad, National Research Council Canada.
   Paper: Saif M. Mohammad, "Obtaining Reliable Human Ratings of Valence,
   Arousal, and Dominance for 20,000 English Words", ACL 2018.
   Home page: http://saifmohammad.com/WebPages/nrc-vad.html

   The NRC terms allow non-commercial research and educational use and
   prohibit redistribution of the lexicon. The full lexicon is not included
   in this package and must not be added back.

   The small JSON files under data/vad_lexicon/ are the pole-word lists
   this demo loads at runtime. Their numeric VAD scores come from the NRC
   lexicon. If you use those scores, cite the NRC VAD paper.

3. Web demo dependencies

   The web/ application depends on React and Vite, installed from npm
   at build time. grimace-main has its own package.json. Those packages
   keep their own licenses and are not vendored as source in this tree,
   except for the Grimace engine described above.
